 "remedyFunctionSource": "def _select_dep_coverages(drel: str, drung: str, source_u: str, want_t: str | None,\n                          inputs: dict, current_subjects: set[str] | None, current_kind: str | None) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Native DEPENDS_ON: reachability\u2192calls@resolved-callee; clones\u2192declares@syntactic.\n\n    Same sourceSubjectKind as the current subject: pair dep Coverage to current-source scopes\n    containing those native ids. Different native kind: whole-source search of (S, T) (all\n    partitions). Never take covs[0]. Unrelated source-subject partitions are not AND-composed\n    into the current view. current_subjects is None for whole-source attestation (all S owed).\n\n    Same kind, the ONLY scopes that can pair are those `_scopes_exact` selects at the exact\n    (dependency relation, dependency rung, S), paired by mapping or commitment exactly as outgoing\n    pairs; there is no mapped-scope fallback (contract section 4). An earlier revision, when no exact\n    scope existed, followed `coverageScopes` to whatever scope record it named and checked only\n    subject membership, so a scope with an absent, null or different sourceUniverse, relation or\n    resolution supplied the dependency and closed `all-covered`. Every scope at the exact coordinates\n    is already in `_scopes_exact`, so that fallback could only pair a scope outside the published\n    selection. Such a scope is now ignored as absent, not refused; a SELECTED scope still refuses on\n    its carrier when paired.\n    \"\"\"\n    covs = _coverages_exact(inputs, drel, drung, source_u, want_t)\n    if not covs:\n        return []\n    dep_kind = _source_kind_for_relation(drel)\n    if current_subjects is None or (current_kind and dep_kind != current_kind):\n        return covs\n    paired, covered = [], set()\n    for sid, sc in _scopes_exact(inputs, drel, drung, source_u):\n        if not any(_scope_contains(sc, nid) for nid in current_subjects):\n            continue\n        found = _pair_scope_coverages(sid, sc, covs, inputs)\n        if found:\n            covered.update(sc.get(\"subjects\") or [])\n        paired.extend(found)\n    if not set(current_subjects) <= covered:\n        return []\n    return _unique_pairs(paired)\n",
